{
  "name": "Schrödinger waveguide array",
  "description": "Linear Schrödinger equation in a periodic potential: 16 parallel channels (V = 0, 10 cells wide) separated by low walls (V = 1.5) the wave can tunnel through. A packet started in one channel leaks sideways channel to channel: discrete diffraction, where the wave runs out in two strong outer lobes with a dark middle, unlike free spreading, which is brightest in the middle. Coupled optical waveguide arrays do exactly this. It starts as a line down one channel, so the spread is all sideways.",
